UnitCLGaugeFactory::constructor
├── when leaf voter is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZA
├── when gauge manager is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZA
├── when voting rewards factory is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZA
├── when nft is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZA
├── when cap admin is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZA
├── when referral admin is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZA
├── when penalty admin is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZA
├── when cap operator is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZA
├── when default cap is zero
│   └── it should revert with ZC
├── when operator min cap is zero
│   └── it should revert with CR
├── when operator min cap exceeds operator max cap
│   └── it should revert with CR
├── when max min stake blocks is less than the default
│   └── it should revert with MS
└── when constructor arguments are valid
    ├── it should set immutable views
    ├── it should set cap views
    ├── it should set referral and penalty defaults
    ├── it should grant initial roles
    └── it should set role admin relationships

UnitCLGaugeFactory::computeGaugeAddress
└── when the pool varies
    └── it should match the independent clone address

UnitCLGaugeFactory::createGauge
├── when the caller is not the gauge manager
│   └── it should revert with NA
└── when the caller is the gauge manager
    ├── when factory data is empty
    │   ├── it should deploy the predicted gauge
    │   ├── it should deploy the voting rewards manager for the predicted gauge
    │   ├── it should initialize gauge fields
    │   ├── it should link the gauge and nft on the pool
    │   ├── it should mark the gauge
    │   ├── it should initialize the emission cap to the current default cap
    │   ├── it should leave referral config empty
    │   └── it should emit GaugeCreated
    ├── when the gauge already exists
    │   └── it should revert on the CREATE2 collision
    ├── when factory data is unknown
    │   ├── it should deploy a gauge
    │   └── it should leave referral config empty
    ├── when factory data is a truncated referral payload
    │   └── it should revert with IR
    ├── when factory data is an oversized referral payload
    │   └── it should revert with IR
    ├── when referral share exceeds max share cap
    │   └── it should revert with SC
    ├── when referral share is nonzero and referral is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with IR
    └── when factory data is referral
        ├── it should deploy a gauge
        ├── it should set referral config
        └── it should emit ReferralConfigSet

UnitCLGaugeFactory::setDefaultCap
├── when the caller does not have the cap admin role
│   └── it should revert with NA
└── when the caller has the cap admin role
    ├── when the cap is zero
    │   └── it should revert with ZC
    └── when the cap is nonzero
        ├── it should update defaultCap
        ├── it should preserve the existing gauge cap
        └── it should emit DefaultCapSet

UnitCLGaugeFactory::setOperatorCapRange
├── when the caller does not have the cap admin role
│   └── it should revert with NA
└── when the caller has the cap admin role
    ├── when min cap is zero
    │   └── it should revert with CR
    ├── when min cap exceeds max cap
    │   └── it should revert with CR
    └── when the range is valid
        ├── it should update operator cap range
        └── it should emit OperatorCapRangeSet

UnitCLGaugeFactory::setEmissionCap
├── when the gauge is invalid
│   └── it should revert with IG
└── when the gauge is valid
    ├── when the caller has the cap admin role
    │   ├── when the cap is zero for cap admin
    │   │   ├── when fee flushing reverts
    │   │   │   └── it should revert with FeeCollectionFailed
    │   │   └── when fee flushing succeeds
    │   │       ├── it should settle the gauge
    │   │       ├── it should flush fees while the prior effective cap is nonzero
    │   │       ├── it should write the zero cap
    │   │       └── it should emit EmissionCapSet
    │   ├── when the cap is the maximum value for cap admin
    │   │   ├── it should settle the gauge
    │   │   ├── it should write the maximum cap
    │   │   └── it should emit EmissionCapSet
    │   └── when the cap is nonzero for cap admin
    │       ├── it should settle the gauge
    │       ├── it should write the cap
    │       └── it should emit EmissionCapSet
    ├── when the caller has the cap operator role
    │   ├── when the current cap is zero
    │   │   └── it should revert with NA
    │   └── when the current cap is nonzero
    │       ├── when the new cap is below the operator range
    │       │   └── it should revert with CR
    │       ├── when the new cap is above the operator range
    │       │   └── it should revert with CR
    │       └── when the new cap is in the operator range
    │           ├── it should settle the gauge
    │           ├── it should write the cap
    │           └── it should emit EmissionCapSet
    ├── when the caller is the emergency council
    │   ├── when the cap is nonzero for emergency council
    │   │   └── it should revert with NA
    │   └── when the cap is zero for emergency council
    │       ├── when fee flushing reverts_
    │       │   └── it should revert with FeeCollectionFailed
    │       └── when fee flushing succeeds_
    │           ├── it should settle the gauge
    │           ├── it should flush fees while the prior effective cap is nonzero
    │           ├── it should write the zero cap
    │           └── it should emit EmissionCapSet
    └── when the caller is not authorized
        └── it should revert with NA

UnitCLGaugeFactory::setEmissionCapRoles
├── when the caller has all roles
│   ├── it should allow setting the emission cap to zero
│   ├── it should allow setting the emission cap within the operator range
│   └── it should allow setting the emission cap to another nonzero value
├── when the caller has the emergency council role
│   ├── when the caller has the cap admin role
│   │   ├── it should allow setting the emission cap to zero
│   │   ├── it should allow setting the emission cap within the operator range
│   │   └── it should allow setting the emission cap to another nonzero value
│   ├── when the caller has the cap operator role
│   │   ├── it should allow setting the emission cap to zero
│   │   ├── it should allow setting the emission cap within the operator range
│   │   └── it should not allow setting the emission cap to another nonzero value
│   └── when the caller has no other role
│       ├── it should allow setting the emission cap to zero
│       ├── it should not allow setting the emission cap within the operator range
│       └── it should not allow setting the emission cap to another nonzero value
├── when the caller has the cap admin role_
│   ├── when the caller has the cap operator role_
│   │   ├── it should allow setting the emission cap to zero
│   │   ├── it should allow setting the emission cap within the operator range
│   │   └── it should allow setting the emission cap to another nonzero value
│   └── when the caller has no other role_
│       ├── it should allow setting the emission cap to zero
│       ├── it should allow setting the emission cap within the operator range
│       └── it should allow setting the emission cap to another nonzero value
└── when the caller has only the cap operator role
    ├── it should not allow setting the emission cap to zero
    ├── it should allow setting the emission cap within the operator range
    └── it should not allow setting the emission cap to another nonzero value

UnitCLGaugeFactory::clearEmissionCap
├── when the gauge is invalid
│   └── it should revert with IG
└── when the gauge is valid
    ├── when the caller is not the emergency council
    │   └── it should revert with NA
    └── when the caller is the emergency council
        ├── when fee flushing reverts
        │   ├── it should settle the gauge
        │   ├── it should attempt to flush fees
        │   ├── it should emit FeeFlushFailed
        │   ├── it should write the zero cap
        │   └── it should emit EmissionCapSet
        └── when fee flushing succeeds
            ├── it should settle the gauge
            ├── it should flush fees while the prior effective cap is nonzero
            ├── it should write the zero cap
            └── it should emit EmissionCapSet

UnitCLGaugeFactory::setMaxShareCap
├── when the caller does not have the referral admin role
│   └── it should revert with NA
└── when the caller has the referral admin role
    ├── when the cap exceeds max pips
    │   └── it should revert with MSC
    └── when the cap is valid
        ├── it should update maxShareCap
        └── it should emit MaxShareCapSet

UnitCLGaugeFactory::setReferralConfig
├── when the caller does not have the referral admin role
│   └── it should revert with NA
└── when the caller has the referral admin role
    ├── when the gauge is invalid
    │   └── it should revert with IG
    ├── when the share exceeds max share cap
    │   └── it should revert with SC
    ├── when share is nonzero and referral is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with IR
    ├── when the config is valid
    │   ├── it should update referral config
    │   └── it should emit ReferralConfigSet
    └── when clearing the config
        ├── it should clear referral config
        └── it should emit ReferralConfigSet

UnitCLGaugeFactory::setPenaltyConfig
├── when the caller does not have the penalty admin role
│   └── it should revert with NA
└── when the caller has the penalty admin role
    ├── when penalty rate exceeds max pips
    │   └── it should revert with MR
    ├── when min stake blocks exceeds max min stake blocks
    │   └── it should revert with MS
    └── when the config is valid
        ├── it should update penaltyConfig
        └── it should emit PenaltyConfigSet

UnitCLGaugeFactory::setMinStakeBlocks
├── when the caller does not have the penalty admin role
│   └── it should revert with NA
└── when the caller has the penalty admin role
    ├── when the gauge is invalid
    │   └── it should revert with IG
    ├── when min stake blocks exceeds max min stake blocks
    │   └── it should revert with MS
    ├── when the override is nonzero
    │   ├── it should update minStakeBlocks
    │   └── it should emit MinStakeBlocksSet
    └── when clearing the override
        ├── it should set minStakeBlocks to the factory default
        └── it should emit MinStakeBlocksSet
